{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"e5dfe802dd66a131","name":"card_unit_wolves_of_tuscany","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Italy/units/card_unit_wolves_of_tuscany","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"WOLVES OF TUSCANY","text":"While this unit is in the frontline, your air units have +2 attack.","flavorText":"The 7th Infantry Division, nicknamed \"Lupi di Toscana\" (e. Wolfs of Tuscany), was a division of the Royal Italian Army in service during WWII. During the war, the division first participated in the Italian invasion of Albania in 1939; and remained stationed there until June 1940 when it returned to Italy and served as part of the army reserve during the Italian invasion of France. Then, the 7th Infantry Division was deployed to Albania in January 1941 as reinforcements during the Greco-Italian War, where it engaged in fierce fighting near Taronine and suffered heavy losses, including the annihilation of one regiment. After regrouping, the division returned to the front in March 1941, participating in defensive and offensive operations, capturing villages and advancing to the Greek-Albanian border by April 1941. Following its return to Italy in October 1941, the division performed coastal defense duties in Calabria and Liguria, and took part in the Axis invasion of Vichy France in November 1942. After the armistice between Italy and the Allied forces in September 1943, the division resisted German forces in Rome for a short while before being disbanded.","faction":"Italy","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_wolves_of_tuscany","title":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_unit_wolves_of_tuscany_title","SourceString":"WOLVES OF TUSCANY","LocalizedString":"WOLVES OF TUSCANY"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":1,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Italy","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_unit_wolves_of_tuscany_text","SourceString":"While this unit is in the frontline, your air units have +2 attack.","LocalizedString":"While this unit is in the frontline, your air units have +2 attack."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_unit_wolves_of_tuscany_history","SourceString":"The 7th Infantry Division, nicknamed \"Lupi di Toscana\" (e. Wolfs of Tuscany), was a division of the Royal Italian Army in service during WWII. During the war, the division first participated in the Italian invasion of Albania in 1939; and remained stationed there until June 1940 when it returned to Italy and served as part of the army reserve during the Italian invasion of France. Then, the 7th Infantry Division was deployed to Albania in January 1941 as reinforcements during the Greco-Italian War, where it engaged in fierce fighting near Taronine and suffered heavy losses, including the annihilation of one regiment. After regrouping, the division returned to the front in March 1941, participating in defensive and offensive operations, capturing villages and advancing to the Greek-Albanian border by April 1941. Following its return to Italy in October 1941, the division performed coastal defense duties in Calabria and Liguria, and took part in the Axis invasion of Vichy France in November 1942. After the armistice between Italy and the Allied forces in September 1943, the division resisted German forces in Rome for a short while before being disbanded.","LocalizedString":"The 7th Infantry Division, nicknamed \"Lupi di Toscana\" (e. Wolfs of Tuscany), was a division of the Royal Italian Army in service during WWII. During the war, the division first participated in the Italian invasion of Albania in 1939; and remained stationed there until June 1940 when it returned to Italy and served as part of the army reserve during the Italian invasion of France. Then, the 7th Infantry Division was deployed to Albania in January 1941 as reinforcements during the Greco-Italian War, where it engaged in fierce fighting near Taronine and suffered heavy losses, including the annihilation of one regiment. After regrouping, the division returned to the front in March 1941, participating in defensive and offensive operations, capturing villages and advancing to the Greek-Albanian border by April 1941. Following its return to Italy in October 1941, the division performed coastal defense duties in Calabria and Liguria, and took part in the Axis invasion of Vichy France in November 1942. After the armistice between Italy and the Allied forces in September 1943, the division resisted German forces in Rome for a short while before being disbanded."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardLocationMoved","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"hasBlitz":true,"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Italy/Mini_Ally_Expansion_25/t_wolves_of_tuscany.t_wolves_of_tuscany","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Italian WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/WOLVES_OF_TUSCANY.WOLVES_OF_TUSCANY","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":361.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_unit_wolves_of_tuscany_photo","SourceString":"Men of the 7th Infantry Division handling an assault mortar. Ca. 1940.","LocalizedString":"Men of the 7th Infantry Division handling an assault mortar. Ca. 1940."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryS'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryS.46"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeLight_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeLight.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_